From fb86c8f2332786188e989477083ce926333ff952 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: terminills <tdeters@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Jul 2026 23:51:36 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 184/638] update_client: identify AROS in component requests
 [chromium] [aros]

Statement:
The portable component update query requires a target OS token and rejected AROS as unknown during the full Chrome build.

Decision:
Report the native platform as aros. Runtime update enablement remains a separate policy decision.

Evidence:
The previously failing update_query_params.o target compiles with x64 architecture and the explicit AROS OS identity.

Chain:

---
 components/update_client/update_query_params.cc | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc b/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc
index 790fc9e5c1..125f455404 100644
--- a/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc
+++ b/components/update_client/update_query_params.cc
@@ -36,6 +36,8 @@ const char kOs[] =
     "android";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS)
     "cros";
+#elif BUILDFLAG(IS_AROS)
+    "aros";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_LINUX) || BUILDFLAG(IS_CHROMEOS_LACROS)
     "linux";
 #elif BUILDFLAG(IS_FUCHSIA)
